&lt;div class="msgHead"&gt; &lt;h1&gt; &lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22Re%5C%3A+%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Intent+to+Ship%5C%3A+Support+for+WebHID%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Support for WebHID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/h1&gt; &lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt; &lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Mike+Taylor%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Mike Taylor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20261030" rel="nofollow"&gt;Fri, 30 Oct 2026 06:37:16 -0700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;If you're just extending WebHID to Android, you don't need LGTMs &lt;/tt&gt;&lt;tt&gt;&lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://www.chromium.org/blink/launching-features/#:~:text=Changes%20which%20extend%20an%20already%20exposed%20API%20to%20additional%20platforms%20without%20introducing%20new%20platform%2Dspecific%20risks%20may%20also%20rely%20just%20on%20a%20PSA%2C%20along%20with%20updating%20the%20ChromeStatus%20entry%20to%20reflect%20the%20new%20platform%20support"&gt;https://www.chromium.org/blink/launching-features/#:~:text=Changes%20which%20extend%20an%20already%20exposed%20API%20to%20additional%20platforms%20without%20introducing%20new%20platform%2Dspecific%20risks%20may%20also%20rely%20just%20on%20a%20PSA%2C%20along%20with%20updating%20the%20ChromeStatus%20entry%20to%20reflect%20the%20new%20platform%20support&lt;/a&gt;.&gt; and &lt;/tt&gt;&lt;tt&gt;this can just be a PSA, but that assumes no meaningful changes between &lt;/tt&gt;&lt;tt&gt;Desktop and Android. Can you confirm? &lt;/tt&gt;&lt;pre style="margin: 0em;"&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;tt&gt;~6 years ago you said &lt;/tt&gt;&lt;tt&gt;&lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/rL1csFYD1Ms/m/g7nxWoROCQAJ"&gt;https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/rL1csFYD1Ms/m/g7nxWoROCQAJ&lt;/a&gt;&gt; &lt;/tt&gt;&lt;tt&gt;you had plans to convert internal tests to WPT exposing a test-only API? &lt;/tt&gt;&lt;tt&gt;(and Mike West encouraged additional WPT coverage). Did that not pan out? &lt;/tt&gt;&lt;pre style="margin: 0em;"&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;tt&gt;Also, &lt;/tt&gt;&lt;tt&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://wpt.fyi/results/webhid?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned"&gt;https://wpt.fyi/results/webhid?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned&lt;/a&gt; - &lt;/tt&gt;&lt;tt&gt;there are two &quot;interface object length&quot; failures. Are those known issues? &lt;/tt&gt;&lt;pre style="margin: 0em;"&gt;
On 10/29/26 9:09 p.m., Chromestatus wrote: &lt;/pre&gt;&lt;blockquote style="border-left: #5555EE solid 0.2em; margin: 0em; padding-left: 0.85em"&gt;&lt;pre style="margin: 0em;"&gt; *Contact emails* &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="8ee3effafafcebf7e0e1a0a0a0cee9e1e1e9e2eba0ede1e3"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="b8d9d4ced1969696f8dfd7d7dfd4dd96dbd7d5"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="fb8994998b928fd5d5d5bb9c94949c979ed5989496"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
