wrote:

&gt; Hi Blink Dev Community,
&gt;
&gt; We're planning to enable an Origin Trial for our web application and would
&gt; appreciate clarification on how the usage restrictions are enforced.
&gt;
&gt; We have two questions:
&gt;
&gt;    1.
&gt;
&gt;    *What counts toward the usage limit?* Is usage measured based on pages
&gt;    receiving a valid Origin-Trial response header, or only when the
&gt;    experimental API is actually invoked? Specifically, can we send the token
&gt;    to all users but restrict actual feature usage to a small subset, or should
&gt;    we limit token distribution itself?
&gt;    2.
&gt;
&gt;    *How is the usage percentage calculated?* Our trial disclosure
&gt;    mentions a 1% usage limit. Is this calculated against our application's
&gt;    traffic, or against total Chrome page loads globally?
&gt;
&gt; Any clarification or pointers to relevant documentation would be greatly
&gt; appreciated.
&gt;
&gt; Thanks!
&gt;
