&lt;pre&gt;Hello Alex,

Sorry for the late reply. Just to make sure I'm addressing what you're
asking:&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

&gt; but I'm wondering if we really have no input from developers?

1. If you mean &quot;Are there any complaints about the current behavior?&quot; –
I've found several discussions highlighting developer pain points:

   -

&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/7838488/how-to-get-the-correct-android-available-screen-height-of-the-browser-in-javascr/8414510"&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/7838488/how-to-get-the-correct-android-available-screen-height-of-the-browser-in-javascr/8414510&lt;/a&gt;

&lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fstackoverflow.com%2Fquestions%2F7838488%2Fhow-to-get-the-correct-android-available-screen-height-of-the-browser-in-javascr%2F8414510"&gt;https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fstackoverflow.com%2Fquestions%2F7838488%2Fhow-to-get-the-correct-android-available-screen-height-of-the-browser-in-javascr%2F8414510&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
   -

&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/12643314/javascript-max-viewport-height-after-orientation-change-android-ios"&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/12643314/javascript-max-viewport-height-after-orientation-change-android-ios&lt;/a&gt;

&lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fstackoverflow.com%2Fquestions%2F12643314%2Fjavascript-max-viewport-height-after-orientation-change-android-ios"&gt;https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fstackoverflow.com%2Fquestions%2F12643314%2Fjavascript-max-viewport-height-after-orientation-change-android-ios&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
