&lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Ftripleodeon.com%2F2011%2F12%2Ffirst-understand-your-screen%2F"&gt;https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Ftripleodeon.com%2F2011%2F12%2Ffirst-understand-your-screen%2F&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
   -

&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/16104434/getting-reliable-available-width-and-height-using-javascript/16166086#16166086"&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/16104434/getting-reliable-available-width-and-height-using-javascript/16166086#16166086&lt;/a&gt;

&lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fstackoverflow.com%2Fquestions%2F16104434%2Fgetting-reliable-available-width-and-height-using-javascript%2F16166086%2316166086"&gt;https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fstackoverflow.com%2Fquestions%2F16104434%2Fgetting-reliable-available-width-and-height-using-javascript%2F16166086%2316166086&lt;/a&gt;&gt;

2. If you mean &quot;Will this break anything?&quot; – The experiment has been
running on Stable for over two months, and we haven't received any bug
reports or negative feedback so far.


