&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;LGTM2

On Mon, Nov 2, 2026 at 3:11 AM Philip Jägenstedt &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="e98f8686c7c7c7a98a819b8684809c84c7869b8e"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
wrote:&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

&gt; LGTM1
&gt;
&gt; Generally it's risky to change exception-throwing to promise-rejection
&gt; since existing try-catch blocks would stop working, but if the only error
&gt; condition is that the document isn't fully active, I agree the risk is very
&gt; small.
&gt;
&gt; On Fri, Oct 30, 2026 at 8:52 PM 'Tommy Steimel' via blink-dev &lt;
&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="87e5ebeee9ecaae3e2f1c7e4eff5e8eaeef2eaa9e8f5e0"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Contact emails*
&gt;&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="61121504084f4f4f210209130e0c08140c4f0e1306"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Explainer*
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/mediasession/pull/312"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/mediasession/pull/312&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Specification*
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://w3c.github.io/mediasession/#dom-mediasession-setmicrophoneactive"&gt;https://w3c.github.io/mediasession/#dom-mediasession-setmicrophoneactive&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Summary*
&gt;&gt; Updates navigator.mediaSession.setMicrophoneActive() and
&gt;&gt; navigator.mediaSession.setCameraActive() to return a Promise&lt;undefined&gt;
&gt;&gt; instead of undefined, matching the W3C Media Session specification. In a
&gt;&gt; fully active document, the returned promise resolves with undefined; if the
&gt;&gt; associated document is not fully active, it returns a promise rejected with
&gt;&gt; an InvalidStateError DOMException.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Blink component*
&gt;&gt; Blink&gt;Media&gt;Session
&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3EMedia%3ESession%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3EMedia%3ESession%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Web Feature ID*
&gt;&gt; media-session &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://webstatus.dev/features/media-session"&gt;https://webstatus.dev/features/media-session&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Motivation*
&gt;&gt; When MediaSession.setMicrophoneActive() and
&gt;&gt; MediaSession.setCameraActive() were originally specified and shipped in
&gt;&gt; Chrome 93, their WebIDL return type was void (undefined). The W3C Media
&gt;&gt; Session specification was subsequently updated (
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/mediasession/pull/312"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/mediasession/pull/312&lt;/a&gt;) so that both methods
&gt;&gt; return Promise&lt;undefined&gt; to support user agents that apply a capture pause
&gt;&gt; policy or prompt the user asynchronously. Updating Chromium's
&gt;&gt; implementation to return Promise&lt;undefined&gt; aligns Chrome with the W3C
&gt;&gt; Media Session specification and fixes 4 failing subtests in WPT's
&gt;&gt; mediasession/idlharness.window.html.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Initial public proposal*
&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *TAG review*
&gt;&gt; N/A — This is a minor spec-compliance update to the return type
&gt;&gt; (undefined -&gt; Promise&lt;undefined&gt;) of two already-shipped MediaSession
&gt;&gt; methods, already specified in the W3C Media Session Working Draft (
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/mediasession/pull/312"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/mediasession/pull/312&lt;/a&gt;) and shipped in Safari.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *TAG review status*
&gt;&gt; Not applicable
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Goals for experimentation*
&gt;&gt; None
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Risks*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Interoperability and Compatibility*
&gt;&gt; Compatibility risk is very low. Existing callers that ignore the return
&gt;&gt; value of setMicrophoneActive() and setCameraActive() are unaffected because
&gt;&gt; the returned promise always resolves with undefined in an active document
&gt;&gt; (so fire-and-forget callers will not encounter unhandled promise
&gt;&gt; rejections). The promise only rejects with InvalidStateError when called on
&gt;&gt; a MediaSession whose associated Document is no longer fully active (such as
&gt;&gt; a detached iframe), or with TypeError when called with too few arguments or
&gt;&gt; an invalid receiver per WebIDL rules for promise-returning operations.
&gt;&gt; Interoperability is improved, as Safari already ships Promise&lt;undefined&gt;
&gt;&gt; for both methods and Firefox is implementing the same WebIDL signature.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Gecko*: Positive (
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/504"&gt;https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/504&lt;/a&gt;)
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *WebKit*: Shipped/Shipping (
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=277421"&gt;https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=277421&lt;/a&gt;) Shipped in Safari 18.4
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Web developers*: No signals N/A — Minor spec-compliance fix to return
&gt;&gt; Promise&lt;undefined&gt; instead of undefined.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Other signals*:
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *WebView application risks*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Does this intent deprecate or change behavior of existing APIs, such that
&gt;&gt; it has potentially high risk for Android WebView-based applications?
&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Debuggability*
&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Will this feature be supported on all six Blink platforms (Windows, Mac,
&gt;&gt; Linux, ChromeOS, Android, and Android WebView)?*
&gt;&gt; Yes
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Is this feature fully tested by web-platform-tests
&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md"&gt;https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md&lt;/a&gt;&gt;?*
&gt;&gt; Yes
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wpt.fyi/results/mediasession/idlharness.window.html"&gt;https://wpt.fyi/results/mediasession/idlharness.window.html&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wpt.fyi/results/mediasession/setmicrophoneactive.html"&gt;https://wpt.fyi/results/mediasession/setmicrophoneactive.html&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wpt.fyi/results/mediasession/setcameraactive.html"&gt;https://wpt.fyi/results/mediasession/setcameraactive.html&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Flag name on about://flags*
&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Finch feature name*
&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Non-finch justification*
&gt;&gt; Changing a WebIDL method's return type from void to Promise&lt;undefined&gt;
&gt;&gt; cannot be guarded behind a runtime feature flag in Blink's generated
&gt;&gt; bindings without changing the IDL return type to 'any' and losing WebIDL's
&gt;&gt; automatic promise-rejection wrapping for invalid arguments/receivers.
&gt;&gt; Compatibility risk is negligible because the returned promise always
&gt;&gt; resolves in an active document.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Rollout plan*
&gt;&gt; Will ship enabled for all users
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Requires code in //chrome?*
&gt;&gt; False
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Tracking bug*
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://crbug.com/576328036"&gt;https://crbug.com/576328036&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Estimated milestones*
&gt;&gt; Shipping on desktop 159
&gt;&gt; Shipping on Android 159
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Anticipated spec changes*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Open questions about a feature may be a source of future web compat or
&gt;&gt; interop issues. Please list open issues (e.g. links to known github issues
&gt;&gt; in the project for the feature specification) whose resolution may
&gt;&gt; introduce web compat/interop risk (e.g., changing to naming or structure of
&gt;&gt; the API in a non-backward-compatible way).
&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;
