&lt;pre&gt;&gt; screen.height - width of system bar + launch bar

I'm sorry screen.height - width of system bar *-* launch bar&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

On Wed, Nov 4, 2026 at 5:38 PM Daniil Hrybchuk &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="0a786f64612424244a6d65656d666f24696567"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:

&gt; Hello Alex,
&gt;
&gt; &gt; the majority of Android devices
&gt; &gt; we'd only be looking to change things on desktop-format Androids
&gt;
&gt; These changes will be rolled out across all Android platforms, though the
&gt; impact will only be visible on desktop devices, as most mobile website
&gt; versions do not use these values.
&gt;
&gt; &gt; And what do we return today for mobile devices for these values?
&gt;
&gt; Without these changes:
&gt;
&gt; 1. screen.availLeft == screen.left
&gt;
&gt; 2. screen.availTop == screen.top
&gt;
&gt; 3. screen.availHeight == screen.height
&gt;
&gt; 4. screen.availWidth == screen.width
&gt;
&gt;
&gt; With these changes
&gt;
&gt; 1. screen.availLeft == screen.left (Currently, no devices have UI elements
&gt; on the sides, but we will account for them if any are introduced.)
&gt;
&gt; 2. screen.availTop == width of system bar
&gt;
&gt; 3. screen.availHeight == screen.height - width of system bar + launch bar
&gt; (on desktop)
&gt;
&gt; 4. screen.availWidth == screen.width (Currently, no devices have UI
&gt; elements on the sides, but we will account for them if any are introduced.)
&gt;
&gt;
&gt;
&gt; &gt;  And are we bringing the behaviour into line with other desktop OSes?
&gt;
&gt; Yes, this is the main reason for these changes.
&gt;
&gt; On Wed, Nov 4, 2026 at 5:25 PM Alex Russell &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="e1928d888689958d98cfcfcfa18289938e8c88948ccf8e9386"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt; wrote:
&gt;
&gt;&gt; Hey Daniil,
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Thanks for all of this. Viewport sizes have indeed been a running problem
&gt;&gt; on mobile, so I'm glad we're improving things in this area.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; We discussed this in today's API OWNERS call, and the major question here
&gt;&gt; is the potential for breakage. If we understand correctly, this won't'
&gt;&gt; really impact the majority of Android devices, and we'd only be looking to
&gt;&gt; change things on desktop-format Androids? And what do we return today for
&gt;&gt; mobile devcies for these values? And are we bringing the behaviour into
&gt;&gt; line with other desktop OSes?
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Thanks,
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Alex
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; On Wednesday, November 4, 2026 at 4:51:58 AM UTC-8 Daniil Hrybchuk wrote:
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Hello Alex,
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Sorry for the late reply. Just to make sure I'm addressing what you're
&gt;&gt;&gt; asking:
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; &gt; but I'm wondering if we really have no input from developers?
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; 1. If you mean &quot;Are there any complaints about the current behavior?&quot; –
&gt;&gt;&gt; I've found several discussions highlighting developer pain points:
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;    -
&gt;&gt;&gt;    
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/7838488/how-to-get-the-correct-android-available-screen-height-of-the-browser-in-javascr/8414510"&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/7838488/how-to-get-the-correct-android-available-screen-height-of-the-browser-in-javascr/8414510&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;    
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fstackoverflow.com%2Fquestions%2F7838488%2Fhow-to-get-the-correct-android-available-screen-height-of-the-browser-in-javascr%2F8414510"&gt;https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fstackoverflow.com%2Fquestions%2F7838488%2Fhow-to-get-the-correct-android-available-screen-height-of-the-browser-in-javascr%2F8414510&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;    -
&gt;&gt;&gt;    
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/12643314/javascript-max-viewport-height-after-orientation-change-android-ios"&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/12643314/javascript-max-viewport-height-after-orientation-change-android-ios&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;    
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fstackoverflow.com%2Fquestions%2F12643314%2Fjavascript-max-viewport-height-after-orientation-change-android-ios"&gt;https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fstackoverflow.com%2Fquestions%2F12643314%2Fjavascript-max-viewport-height-after-orientation-change-android-ios&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;    - &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://tripleodeon.com/2011/12/first-understand-your-screen/"&gt;https://tripleodeon.com/2011/12/first-understand-your-screen/&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;    
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Ftripleodeon.com%2F2011%2F12%2Ffirst-understand-your-screen%2F"&gt;https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Ftripleodeon.com%2F2011%2F12%2Ffirst-understand-your-screen%2F&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;    -
&gt;&gt;&gt;    
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/16104434/getting-reliable-available-width-and-height-using-javascript/16166086#16166086"&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/16104434/getting-reliable-available-width-and-height-using-javascript/16166086#16166086&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;    
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fstackoverflow.com%2Fquestions%2F16104434%2Fgetting-reliable-available-width-and-height-using-javascript%2F16166086%2316166086"&gt;https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fstackoverflow.com%2Fquestions%2F16104434%2Fgetting-reliable-available-width-and-height-using-javascript%2F16166086%2316166086&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; 2. If you mean &quot;Will this break anything?&quot; – The experiment has been
&gt;&gt;&gt; running on Stable for over two months, and we haven't received any bug
&gt;&gt;&gt; reports or negative feedback so far.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; On Wed, Oct 21, 2026 at 5:32 PM Alex Russell &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="f3809f9a949b879f8addddddb3909b819c9e9a869edd9c8194"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; This feels like a useful change, but I'm wondering if we really have no
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; input from developers?
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; On Wednesday, October 21, 2026 at 3:37:20 AM UTC-7 Chromestatus wrote:
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Contact emails*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="6113040f0a4f4f4f21060e0e060d044f020e0c"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Explainer*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Screen"&gt;https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Screen&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Specification*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Screen"&gt;https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Screen&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Design docs*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1AccF_jc0ZgnM10YZSRzMjoTyJefKUH1A4OwaDcm1s9Y"&gt;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1AccF_jc0ZgnM10YZSRzMjoTyJefKUH1A4OwaDcm1s9Y&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Summary*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; The screen.avail properties account for system UI elements when
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; calculating available screen space on Android. This provides developers
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; with the exact usable display area needed to accurately place application
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; windows on Android.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Blink component*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Blink&gt;Screen
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3EScreen%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3EScreen%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Web Feature ID*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; screen &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://webstatus.dev/features/screen"&gt;https://webstatus.dev/features/screen&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Motivation*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; These changes in screen.avail properties provide developers with the
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; exact usable display area needed to accurately place application windows.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Consequently, popups and windows appear in the correct locations without
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; overlapping the operating system interface.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Initial public proposal*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *TAG review*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *TAG review status*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Not applicable
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Goals for experimentation*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; None
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Risks*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Interoperability and Compatibility*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Gecko*: No signal
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *WebKit*: No signal
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Web developers*: No signals
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Other signals*:
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *WebView application risks*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Does this intent deprecate or change behavior of existing APIs, such
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; that it has potentially high risk for Android WebView-based applications?
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
