&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Alex+Russell%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Alex Russell&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20261104" rel="nofollow"&gt;Wed, 04 Nov 2026 09:12:34 -0800&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;Why aren't we shipping? OT shouldn't be used as a soft-launch vehicle, so 
if we aren't going to learn anything here and the IETF conversation is only 
about the colour of the bikeshed, I'd rather we remove our trial and wait 
on consensus, or ship and force the issue.&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

Best,

Alex

