&lt;div class="msgHead"&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;
&lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22Re%5C%3A+%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Intent+to+Ship%5C%3A+Web+Bluetooth%5C%3A+BluetoothRemoteGATTServer.maxWriteWithoutResponseSize%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Web Bluetooth: BluetoothRemoteGATTServer.maxWriteWithoutResponseSize&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Rick+Byers%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Rick Byers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20261104" rel="nofollow"&gt;Wed, 04 Nov 2026 09:14:06 -0800&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;LGTM3. But let us know if landing the specs and tests gets blocked for some
reason - worst case we can approve proceeding based on the PRs, but we
should make an honest effort to try to get the PRs landed.&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

On Wed, Nov 4, 2026 at 11:16 AM Philip Jägenstedt &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="50363f3f7e7e7e103338223f3d39253d7e3f2237"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
wrote:

&gt; Hey Helmut,
&gt;
&gt; Since you have a plan for finishing the spec and tests, we don't need to
&gt; pause the thread. Instead:
&gt;
&gt; LGTM2 assuming spec and tests are merged before flipping the flag.
&gt;
&gt; It's great to see BiDi automation in practice here, Bluetooth was for a
&gt; long time the my go-to example of a feature that was too complex to test
&gt; using WPT, and that's no longer true! 🎉
&gt;
&gt; On Mon, Nov 2, 2026 at 7:54 PM Helmut Januschka &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="fb93919a958e8898d5d5d5bb9c969a9297d5989496"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt; wrote:
&gt;
&gt;&gt; Tests are done, and they're real WPTs, not Chromium-only ones.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; They drive the simulated peripheral over WebDriver BiDi, so any
&gt;&gt; implementation with the Bluetooth automation module can run them.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; That needed two upstream pieces, both up now:
&gt;&gt; - spec text for the bluetooth.simulateGattMtuChange automation command,
&gt;&gt; folded into the existing PR: &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/whatwg/bluetooth/pull/672"&gt;https://github.com/whatwg/bluetooth/pull/672&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt; (hope it will merge soon)
&gt;&gt; - the testdriver/wptrunner plumbing for it:
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/64568"&gt;https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/64568&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Chromium side: &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://crrev.com/c/8701256"&gt;https://crrev.com/c/8701256&lt;/a&gt; (emulation),
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://crrev.com/c/8701565"&gt;https://crrev.com/c/8701565&lt;/a&gt; (BiDi command), &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://crrev.com/c/8702715"&gt;https://crrev.com/c/8702715&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt; (the tests).
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; hope that's the right path, still a noobie here, should i now try to get
&gt;&gt; all PR's and CL's green/reviewed and after that, we continue with the LGTM
&gt;&gt; collection?
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; cheers,
&gt;&gt; helmut
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Philip Jägenstedt schrieb am Mittwoch, 28. Oktober 2026 um 16:29:12 UTC+1:
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Adding those tests would be great, I'm glad to hear it's feasible!
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Can &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/whatwg/bluetooth/pull/672"&gt;https://github.com/whatwg/bluetooth/pull/672&lt;/a&gt; be merged now that the
&gt;&gt;&gt; spec has moved to the WHATWG?
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; On Tue, Oct 27, 2026 at 7:56 PM Alex Russell &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="afdcc3c6c8c7818181efccc7ddc0c2c6dac281c0ddc8"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; LGTM1 on the condition that tests land soon; not a ship blocker, but
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; within the next month would be best as others are looking at implementing
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; WebBT and tests are the best guide.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Best,
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Alex
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; On Wednesday, October 21, 2026 at 4:24:35 PM UTC-7 &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="c8a0a2a9a6bde6e6e688afa5a9a1a4e6aba7a5"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Please file a Mozilla standards request for this feature.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Filed: &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/1473"&gt;https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/1473&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; will update feature entry as soon theres a response.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Could a WPT be added for this?
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Not today. Web Bluetooth WPTs drive fake peripherals through the
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; bluetooth BiDi module in the spec’s Automated testing
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://webbluetoothcg.github.io/web-bluetooth/#automated-testing"&gt;https://webbluetoothcg.github.io/web-bluetooth/#automated-testing&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; section, and neither those bluetooth.simulate* commands nor
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Chromium’s FakeCentral/FakePeripheral know anything about ATT_MTU. A
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; fake device therefore always sits at the default, so there is nothing a
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; test could assert.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Making it testable means an mtu on the GATT connection response plus
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; a simulateGattMtuChange command, specced in that Automated testing
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; section and implemented in the Chromium emulation layer. Happy to do all 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; of
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; it. How would you like it, land the automation commands in the spec first
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; and have the WPTs as a shipping blocker, or ship on the current unit test
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; coverage (web_bluetooth_service_impl_unittest.cc,
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; bluetooth_gatt_bluez_unittest.cc, global-interface-listing) and track
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; the WPTs as a follow-up?
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
