&lt;h1&gt;
&lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22Re%5C%3A+%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Intent+to+Ship%5C%3A+WebTransport+connection+statistics%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: WebTransport connection statistics&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Alex+Russell%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Alex Russell&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20261109" rel="nofollow"&gt;Mon, 09 Nov 2026 11:33:52 -0800&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;LGTM2

On Thursday, November 5, 2026 at 11:50:20 AM UTC-8 &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="fe9a9f90d0d0d0be93979d8c918d91988ad09d9193"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt; 
wrote:&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

&gt; LGTM1
&gt;
&gt;  
&gt;
&gt; *From:* &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="5e3c32373035733a3b281e3d362c3133372b3370312c39"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt; &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="395b55505752145d5c4f795a514b5654504c5417564b5e"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; *On Behalf Of *
&gt; Chromestatus
&gt; *Sent:* Thursday, November 5, 2026 9:37 AM
&gt; *To:* &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="6507090c0b0e4801001325060d170a080c10084b0a1702"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
&gt; *Cc:* Daniel Clark &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="b8dcd9d6969696f8d5d1dbcad7cbd7decc96dbd7d5"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="d7a5bef9f9f997b0b8b8b0bbb2f9b4b8ba"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;; 
&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="56253a3f313e223a2f78787816353e24393b3f233b78392431"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;; Viktoriya Bryhider &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="87f1e5f5feefeea9a9a9c7eaeee4f5e8f4e8e1f3a9e4e8ea"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt; *Subject:* [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: WebTransport connection statistics
&gt;
&gt;  
&gt;
&gt; *Contact emails*
&gt;
&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="631501111a0b0a4d4d4d230e0a00110c100c05174d000c0e"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Explainer*
&gt;
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/webtransport/blob/main/explainer.md#stats"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/webtransport/blob/main/explainer.md#stats&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Specification*
&gt;
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://w3c.github.io/webtransport/#dictdef-webtransportconnectionstats"&gt;https://w3c.github.io/webtransport/#dictdef-webtransportconnectionstats&lt;/a&gt; 
&gt;
&gt; *Design docs*
&gt;
&gt;
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/WebTransport/getStats"&gt;https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/WebTransport/getStats&lt;/a&gt;
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://w3c.github.io/webtransport/#web-transport-connection-stats"&gt;https://w3c.github.io/webtransport/#web-transport-connection-stats&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Summary*
&gt;
&gt; WebTransport.getStats() provides asynchronous statistics for an existing 
&gt; connection: round-trip time measurements when available, an estimated 
&gt; sending rate when available, and counts of expired, lost, and dropped 
&gt; datagrams. Statistics remain accessible after the connection closes. 
&gt; Chromium does not currently expose connection byte or packet totals. 
&gt;
&gt; *Blink component*
&gt;
&gt; Blink&gt;Network&gt;WebTransport 
&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ENetwork%3EWebTransport%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ENetwork%3EWebTransport%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Web Feature ID*
&gt;
&gt; webtransport &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://webstatus.dev/features/webtransport"&gt;https://webstatus.dev/features/webtransport&lt;/a&gt;&gt; 
&gt;
&gt; *Motivation*
&gt;
&gt; WebTransport applications need to distinguish connection latency, 
&gt; congestion, and datagram loss or expiration from application-side delays. A 
&gt; single asynchronous call exposes a snapshot of the existing connection's 
&gt; health to help developers adapt sending behavior and troubleshoot problems. 
&gt; It does not create a connection or change how application data is 
&gt; transmitted. 
&gt;
&gt; *Initial public proposal*
&gt;
&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;
&gt; *TAG review*
&gt;
&gt;
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1212#issuecomment-5071009850"&gt;https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1212#issuecomment-5071009850&lt;/a&gt; 
&gt;
&gt; *TAG review status*
&gt;
&gt; Issues addressed
&gt;
&gt; *Goals for experimentation*
&gt;
&gt; None 
&gt;
&gt; *Risks*
&gt;
&gt;  
&gt;
&gt; *Interoperability and Compatibility*
&gt;
&gt; This is an additive method on an existing WebTransport object: existing 
&gt; code is unaffected if it does not use the new method. Developers must check 
&gt; for method support and handle a rejection or missing dictionary members 
&gt; when working across browsers. Firefox and Safari expose getStats(), but 
&gt; implementation maturity and returned fields vary between all browsers. The 
&gt; WebTransport specification currently defines connection byte/packet 
&gt; counters (bytesSent, bytesSentOverhead, bytesAcknowledged, packetsSent, 
&gt; bytesLost, packetsLost, bytesReceived, packetsReceived) and atSendCapacity; 
&gt; Chromium does not expose these members. Applications should check for 
&gt; optional members rather than assume that every browser returns the same 
&gt; subset. 
&gt;
&gt; *Gecko*: Shipped/Shipping (
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Firefox/Releases/158#apis"&gt;https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Firefox/Releases/158#apis&lt;/a&gt;) 
&gt; WebTransport.getStats() 
&gt; shipped in Firefox 158, released October 13, 2026.
&gt;
&gt; *WebKit*: Shipped/Shipping (
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/WebKit-7625.2.8/Source/WebKit/NetworkProcess/webtransport/cocoa/NetworkTransportSessionCocoa.mm#L410-L413"&gt;https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/WebKit-7625.2.8/Source/WebKit/NetworkProcess/webtransport/cocoa/NetworkTransportSessionCocoa.mm#L410-L413&lt;/a&gt;)
&gt;  Safari 
&gt; 27.2 exposes  WebTransport.getStats(), but its WebKit(7625.2.8) 
&gt; implementation returns default-initialized connection statistics. WebKit 
&gt; main has since added bytesSent and bytesReceived counters.
&gt;
&gt; *Web developers*: Positive (
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/web-platform-tests/interop/issues/1121"&gt;https://github.com/web-platform-tests/interop/issues/1121&lt;/a&gt;) The Interop 
&gt; 2026 WebTransport proposal received 28 positive reactions. Developers also 
&gt; reported active WebTransport use and significant cross-engine differences.
&gt;
&gt; *Other signals*:
&gt;
&gt; *Ergonomics*
&gt;
&gt; Values are asynchronous snapshots, not continuously updated measurements. 
&gt; RTT fields are in milliseconds; estimatedSendRate is in bits per second and 
&gt; can be null when no estimate is available.
&gt;
&gt; *Activation*
&gt;
&gt; There is no distinct activation risk identified for 
&gt; WebTransport.getStats(). Enabling it exposes an additive method; sites that 
&gt; do not call it keep their existing WebTransport behavior.
&gt;
&gt; *Security*
&gt;
&gt; The method returns aggregate connection information for a WebTransport 
&gt; object the caller already owns; it does not disclose payloads or peer 
&gt; credentials and does not add a new connection capability. RTT and estimated 
&gt; send rate can reveal characteristics of a user's network and help 
&gt; fingerprint or correlate activity. The WebTransport spec limits disclosure 
&gt; of connection and datagram counters on connections subject to pooling while 
&gt; permitting selected pooled-connection measurements such as RTT and 
&gt; estimated send rate.
&gt;
&gt; *WebView application risks*
&gt;
&gt; *Does this intent deprecate or change behavior of existing APIs, such that 
&gt; it has potentially high risk for Android WebView-based applications? *
&gt;
&gt; Low. This is an additive API on existing WebTransport API and does not 
&gt; change connection establishment or network behavior. 
&gt;
&gt;  
&gt;
&gt; *Debuggability*
&gt;
&gt; Applications can inspect getStats() results from script or the DevTools 
&gt; Console. No dedicated DevTools connection-statistics UI is required for the 
&gt; API to work. 
&gt;
&gt; *Will this feature be supported on all six Blink platforms (Windows, Mac, 
&gt; Linux, ChromeOS, Android, and Android WebView)?*
&gt;
&gt; Yes
&gt;
&gt; *Is this feature fully tested by web-platform-tests 
&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md"&gt;https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md&lt;/a&gt;&gt;?*
&gt;
&gt; Yes 
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wpt.fyi/results/webtransport/stats.https.any.html"&gt;https://wpt.fyi/results/webtransport/stats.https.any.html&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Flag name on about://flags*
&gt;
&gt; enable-experimental-web-platform-features 
&gt;
&gt; *Finch feature name*
&gt;
&gt; WebTransportStats 
&gt;
&gt; *Rollout plan*
&gt;
&gt; Will ship enabled for all users
&gt;
&gt; *Requires code in //chrome?*
&gt;
&gt; False
&gt;
&gt; *Tracking bug*
&gt;
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues/573538454"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues/573538454&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Availability expectation*
&gt;
&gt; Firefox 158 and Safari 26.4 expose WebTransport.getStats(), although 
&gt; implementation maturity and available dictionary fields differ. 
&gt;
&gt; *Adoption expectation*
&gt;
&gt; Adoption is expected primarily among WebTransport applications that 
&gt; monitor network performance or datagram delivery.
&gt;
&gt; *Non-OSS dependencies*
&gt;
&gt; *Does the feature depend on any code or APIs outside the Chromium open 
&gt; source repository and its open-source dependencies to function? *
&gt;
&gt; No
&gt;
&gt; *Estimated milestones*
&gt;
&gt; Shipping on desktop
&gt;
&gt; 159
&gt;
&gt; DevTrial on desktop
&gt;
&gt; 124
&gt;
&gt; Shipping on Android
&gt;
&gt; 159
&gt;
&gt; DevTrial on Android
&gt;
&gt; 124
&gt;
&gt; Shipping on WebView
&gt;
&gt; 159
&gt;
&gt;  
&gt;
&gt; *Anticipated spec changes*
&gt;
&gt; *Open questions about a feature may be a source of future web compat or 
&gt; interop issues. Please list open issues (e.g. links to known github issues 
&gt; in the project for the feature specification) whose resolution may 
&gt; introduce web compat/interop risk (e.g., changing to naming or structure of 
&gt; the API in a non-backward-compatible way). *
&gt;
&gt; None known.
&gt;
&gt; *Link to entry on the Chrome Platform Status*
&gt;
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5120203192139776?gate=5581427851788288"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/feature/5120203192139776?gate=5581427851788288&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; This intent message was generated by Chrome Platform Status 
&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/&lt;/a&gt;&gt;. 
&gt;
&gt; -- 
&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups 
&gt; &quot;blink-dev&quot; group.
&gt; To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an 
&gt; email to &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="accec0c5c2c781c8c9da87d9c2dfd9cedfcfde828282eccfc4dec3c1c5d9c182c3decb"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;.
&gt; To view this discussion visit 
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msgid/blink-dev/6aecbed8.dafb4d6f.4865.0071.GAE%40google.com"&gt;https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msgid/blink-dev/6aecbed8.dafb4d6f.4865.0071.GAE%40google.com&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;  
&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msgid/blink-dev/6aecbed8.dafb4d6f.4865.0071.GAE%40google.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer"&gt;https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msgid/blink-dev/6aecbed8.dafb4d6f.4865.0071.GAE%40google.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt; .
&gt;

