&lt;div class="msgHead"&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;
&lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Re%5C%3A+Intent+to+Ship%5C%3A+Account+for+System+UI+elements+in+screen.avail+properties+on+Android%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;[blink-dev] Re: Intent to Ship: Account for System UI elements in screen.avail properties on Android&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Alex+Russell%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Alex Russell&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20261109" rel="nofollow"&gt;Mon, 09 Nov 2026 11:34:48 -0800&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;Thanks, that scopes down the risk considerably. LGTM1

On Wednesday, November 4, 2026 at 8:42:23 AM UTC-8 Daniil Hrybchuk wrote:&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

&gt; &gt; screen.height - width of system bar + launch bar
&gt;
&gt; I'm sorry screen.height - width of system bar *-* launch bar
&gt;
&gt; On Wed, Nov 4, 2026 at 5:38 PM Daniil Hrybchuk &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="b4c6d1dadf9a9a9af4d3dbdbd3d8d19ad7dbd9"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;
&gt;&gt; Hello Alex,
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; &gt; the majority of Android devices
&gt;&gt; &gt; we'd only be looking to change things on desktop-format Androids
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; These changes will be rolled out across all Android platforms, though the 
&gt;&gt; impact will only be visible on desktop devices, as most mobile website 
&gt;&gt; versions do not use these values.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; &gt; And what do we return today for mobile devices for these values?
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Without these changes:
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; 1. screen.availLeft == screen.left
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; 2. screen.availTop == screen.top
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; 3. screen.availHeight == screen.height
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; 4. screen.availWidth == screen.width
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; With these changes
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; 1. screen.availLeft == screen.left (Currently, no devices have UI 
&gt;&gt; elements on the sides, but we will account for them if any are introduced.)
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; 2. screen.availTop == width of system bar
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; 3. screen.availHeight == screen.height - width of system bar + launch bar 
&gt;&gt; (on desktop)
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; 4. screen.availWidth == screen.width (Currently, no devices have UI 
&gt;&gt; elements on the sides, but we will account for them if any are introduced.)
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; &gt;  And are we bringing the behaviour into line with other desktop OSes?
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Yes, this is the main reason for these changes.
&gt;&gt;
