&lt;pre&gt;LGTM2

On Monday, November 9, 2026 at 11:34:38 AM UTC-8 &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="ef9c83868887c1c1c1af8c879d8082869a82c1809d88"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt; 
wrote:&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

&gt; Thanks, that scopes down the risk considerably. LGTM1
&gt;
&gt; On Wednesday, November 4, 2026 at 8:42:23 AM UTC-8 Daniil Hrybchuk wrote:
&gt;
&gt;&gt; &gt; screen.height - width of system bar + launch bar
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; I'm sorry screen.height - width of system bar *-* launch bar
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; On Wed, Nov 4, 2026 at 5:38 PM Daniil Hrybchuk &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="0674636828282846616969616a632865696b"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Hello Alex,
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; &gt; the majority of Android devices
&gt;&gt;&gt; &gt; we'd only be looking to change things on desktop-format Androids
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; These changes will be rolled out across all Android platforms, though 
&gt;&gt;&gt; the impact will only be visible on desktop devices, as most mobile website 
&gt;&gt;&gt; versions do not use these values.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; &gt; And what do we return today for mobile devices for these values?
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Without these changes:
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; 1. screen.availLeft == screen.left
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; 2. screen.availTop == screen.top
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; 3. screen.availHeight == screen.height
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; 4. screen.availWidth == screen.width
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; With these changes
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; 1. screen.availLeft == screen.left (Currently, no devices have UI 
&gt;&gt;&gt; elements on the sides, but we will account for them if any are introduced.)
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; 2. screen.availTop == width of system bar
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; 3. screen.availHeight == screen.height - width of system bar + launch 
&gt;&gt;&gt; bar (on desktop)
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; 4. screen.availWidth == screen.width (Currently, no devices have UI 
&gt;&gt;&gt; elements on the sides, but we will account for them if any are introduced.)
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; &gt;  And are we bringing the behaviour into line with other desktop OSes?
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Yes, this is the main reason for these changes.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; On Wed, Nov 4, 2026 at 5:25 PM Alex Russell &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="43302f2a242b6d6d6d03202b312c2e2a362e6d2c3124"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Hey Daniil,
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Thanks for all of this. Viewport sizes have indeed been a running 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; problem on mobile, so I'm glad we're improving things in this area.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; We discussed this in today's API OWNERS call, and the major question 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; here is the potential for breakage. If we understand correctly, this 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; won't' 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; really impact the majority of Android devices, and we'd only be looking to 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; change things on desktop-format Androids? And what do we return today for 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; mobile devcies for these values? And are we bringing the behaviour into 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; line with other desktop OSes?
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Thanks,
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Alex
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; On Wednesday, November 4, 2026 at 4:51:58 AM UTC-8 Daniil Hrybchuk 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Hello Alex,
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Sorry for the late reply. Just to make sure I'm addressing what you're 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; asking:
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &gt; but I'm wondering if we really have no input from developers?
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; 1. If you mean &quot;Are there any complaints about the current behavior?&quot; – 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; I've found several discussions highlighting developer pain points:
