&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22%27Isaac+Ahouma%27+via+blink%5C-dev%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;'Isaac Ahouma' via blink-dev&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20261109" rel="nofollow"&gt;Mon, 09 Nov 2026 11:45:24 -0800&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;Thanks Jeffrey! That makes sense. I have opened a focused TAG review for
the samplingMode design here and updated ChromeStatus accordingly:
&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1308"&gt;https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1308&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

Best,
Isaac

On Mon, Nov 9, 2026 at 10:42 AM Jeffrey Yasskin &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="4d27342c3e3e6363630d2e253f222024382063223f2a"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
wrote:

&gt; On Mon, Nov 9, 2026 at 10:24 AM Chromestatus &lt;
&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="7110155f5f5f3112035c0205100504025f10010102011e051c10181d5f121e1c"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;
&gt;&gt; *TAG review*
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1093"&gt;https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1093&lt;/a&gt; This update
&gt;&gt; directly addresses the TAG’s Prompt API early design review feedback on
&gt;&gt; “Interoperable model parameters”. We adopted TAG guidance by replacing raw
&gt;&gt; hyperparameters with samplingMode presets, which enable user agents to map
&gt;&gt; semantic developer intent to model-specific sampling configurations.
&gt;&gt; Because this incremental refinement directly fulfills prior TAG advice
&gt;&gt; rather than a new architectural surface, a separate review is not merited.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;
&gt; Even though you're implementing a goal the TAG expressed, the TAG may
&gt; still have feedback on _how_ you're implementing it. I can't promise that
&gt; we'll give timely feedback, but I think it's still worth sending a review
&gt; for this.
&gt;
&gt; Thanks,
&gt; Jeffrey
&gt;

