&lt;div class="msgHead"&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;
&lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Re%5C%3A+Intent+to+Ship%5C%3A+SpeechRecognitionResult+Timestamps+%5C%28WebSpeech+API%5C%29%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;[blink-dev] Re: Intent to Ship: SpeechRecognitionResult Timestamps (WebSpeech API)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Alex+Russell%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Alex Russell&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20261109" rel="nofollow"&gt;Mon, 09 Nov 2026 12:04:44 -0800&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;Hey Alan,

This is a great feature.&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

We try not to take statement of positive intent as official browser signals 
as other vendors have requested we not do that, and instead use their 
formal channels. I know that's more paperwork, but we do not want to cause 
trouble for the line engineers at our friendly partners on other browser 
teams by putting them in the spotlight in ways that are out of sync with 
their leadership.

LGTM1, conditional on filing explicit signals requests through the formal 
channels (but not conditional on their response).

Godspeed,

Alex

On Friday, November 6, 2026 at 2:17:12 PM UTC-8 Alan Ding wrote:

&gt; Contact emails
&gt;
&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="43222f222d276d6d6d03202b312c2e2a362e6d2c3124"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; Explainer
&gt;
&gt;
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WebAudio/web-speech-api/blob/main/explainers/speech-recognition-result-timestamps.md"&gt;https://github.com/WebAudio/web-speech-api/blob/main/explainers/speech-recognition-result-timestamps.md&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; Specification
&gt;
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://webaudio.github.io/web-speech-api/#speechreco-result"&gt;https://webaudio.github.io/web-speech-api/#speechreco-result&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; Summary
&gt;
&gt; The Web Speech API currently does not expose the acoustic timing bounds of 
&gt; recognized speech segments, making it difficult to associate transcribed 
&gt; text with media timelines or generate synchronized subtitle cues. We 
&gt; propose adding speechStartTime and speechEndTime (double, in seconds 
&gt; relative to stream start) attributes on the SpeechRecognitionResult 
&gt; interface.
&gt;
&gt; Blink component
&gt;
&gt; Blink&gt;Speech 
&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ESpeech%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ESpeech%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;
&gt; Web Feature ID
&gt;
&gt; speech-recognition &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://webstatus.dev/features/speech-recognition"&gt;https://webstatus.dev/features/speech-recognition&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;
&gt; Motivation
&gt;
&gt; The Web Speech API currently does not expose the acoustic start and end 
&gt; timestamps of recognized speech utterances on SpeechRecognitionResult. 
&gt; While SpeechRecognitionEvent.timeStamp conveys when the DOM event occurred, 
&gt; it provides no information about the acoustic boundaries or duration of the 
&gt; speech segment within the source audio stream. Exposing speechStartTime and 
&gt; speechEndTime (in seconds as a double, matching 
&gt; HTMLMediaElement.currentTime, BaseAudioContext.currentTime, and VTTCue) 
&gt; addresses critical media timeline association capabilities that are 
&gt; currently impossible on the web: 
&gt;
&gt; 1. Automated Subtitling &amp; Caption Tracks: Constructing frame-accurate 
&gt; subtitle cues (VTTCue(start, end, text)) for recorded or streaming 
&gt; audio/video. 
&gt;
&gt; 2. Interactive &quot;Click-to-Seek&quot; Navigation: Enabling users to click a 
&gt; phrase in a transcript and immediately seek playback to the exact moment it 
&gt; was spoken. 
&gt;
&gt; 3. Conferencing &amp; Media Recording Alignment: Synchronizing real-time 
&gt; captions with recorded media tracks or WebRTC playout delay buffers.
&gt;
&gt; 4. Text-Based Media Editing: Accurately cutting, splicing, or rearranging 
&gt; audio and video based on transcript text.
&gt;
&gt; Initial public proposal
&gt;
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WebAudio/web-speech-api/issues/191"&gt;https://github.com/WebAudio/web-speech-api/issues/191&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; TAG review
&gt;
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1267"&gt;https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1267&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; TAG review status
&gt;
&gt; Issues addressed
&gt;
&gt; Risks
&gt;
&gt; Interoperability and Compatibility
&gt;
&gt; Low interoperability and compatibility risk. This is a purely additive 
&gt; change introducing two read-only double attributes (speechStartTime and 
&gt; speechEndTime) on SpeechRecognitionResult, along with updating 
&gt; SpeechRecognitionEvent.timeStamp to reflect the end of the recognized 
&gt; speech segment on the session audio timeline. Existing applications using 
&gt; SpeechRecognition continue to work without modification, and developers can 
&gt; feature-detect support via 'speechStartTime' in 
&gt; SpeechRecognitionResult.prototype. The specification update (
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WebAudio/web-speech-api/pull/192"&gt;https://github.com/WebAudio/web-speech-api/pull/192&lt;/a&gt;) was shaped by 
&gt; feedback from the W3C Audio Working Group / Community Group (including 
&gt; @padenot at Mozilla) and the W3C TAG (
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1267"&gt;https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1267&lt;/a&gt;).
&gt;
&gt; Gecko: No signal (&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WebAudio/web-speech-api/pull/192"&gt;https://github.com/WebAudio/web-speech-api/pull/192&lt;/a&gt;) 
&gt; Unofficial approval from @padenot (Mozilla) on spec update.
&gt;
&gt; WebKit: No signal
&gt;
&gt; Web developers: Positive (
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WebAudio/web-speech-api/issues/191"&gt;https://github.com/WebAudio/web-speech-api/issues/191&lt;/a&gt;) Requested by 
&gt; internal and external web developers building real-time captioning, media 
&gt; recording alignment, and latency-sensitive conferencing applications 
&gt; (including Google Meet). For example, speechStartTime and speechEndTime are 
&gt; used to generate synchronized VTTCue captions and interactive click-to-seek 
&gt; transcripts and developer specifically needed this feature to properly map 
&gt; results to the timeline to know when the speech that generated the text in 
&gt; the result started and ended for applications such as Subtitling &amp; Closed 
&gt; Captions, Meeting Transcripts, Live WebRTC Video Sync (see 
&gt; crbug.com/551992211#comment3).
&gt;
&gt; Other signals:
&gt;
&gt; WebView application risks
&gt;
&gt; Does this intent deprecate or change behavior of existing APIs, such that 
&gt; it has potentially high risk for Android WebView-based applications?
&gt;
&gt; None. This feature only adds new read-only attributes to 
&gt; SpeechRecognitionResult and does not deprecate or break existing APIs. 
&gt; Furthermore, the Web Speech API (SpeechRecognition) is not supported on 
&gt; Android WebView.
&gt;
&gt; Debuggability
&gt;
&gt; No special DevTools support is needed. speechStartTime and speechEndTime 
&gt; are standard read-only IDL attributes exposed on SpeechRecognitionResult 
&gt; instances (and timeStamp on SpeechRecognitionEvent) and can be inspected 
&gt; directly in the DevTools Console, Scope pane, and watch expressions like 
&gt; any other DOM object properties.
&gt;
&gt; Will this feature be supported on all six Blink platforms (Windows, Mac, 
&gt; Linux, ChromeOS, Android, and Android WebView)?
&gt;
&gt; No
&gt;
&gt; Supported on desktop platforms (Windows, Mac, Linux, and ChromeOS). Not 
&gt; currently supported on Android or Android WebView: Android WebView does not 
&gt; support the SpeechRecognition API, and Chrome on Android delegates to the 
&gt; OS-level Android SpeechRecognizer service, which does not expose 
&gt; segment-level start and end timestamps. The WebSpeechTimestamps runtime 
&gt; feature flag will only be enabled on desktop platforms (Windows, Mac, 
&gt; Linux, and ChromeOS), leaving speechStartTime and speechEndTime unexposed 
&gt; on Android and Android WebView.
&gt;
&gt; Is this feature fully tested by web-platform-tests 
&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md"&gt;https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt; ?
&gt;
&gt; No
&gt;
&gt; End-to-end Web Speech API recognition tests cannot currently run in 
&gt; automated Web Platform Tests (WPT) because WPT lacks a WebDriver mock 
&gt; speech recognition backend automation hook (and on-device recognition 
&gt; models are not bundled in standard WPT test runners). The IDL surface is 
&gt; covered by WPT idlharness tests, and the timestamp exposure, 2ms 
&gt; quantization (FuzzTimestamp), and SpeechRecognitionEvent.timeStamp rebasing 
&gt; are covered by Blink unit tests 
&gt; (third_party/blink/renderer/modules/speech/speech_recognition_test.cc, 
&gt; crrev.com/c/8409366 and crrev.com/c/8729884) as well as browser/service 
&gt; unit tests 
&gt; (content/browser/speech/soda_speech_recognition_engine_impl_unittest.cc, 
&gt; content/browser/speech/on_device_speech_recognition_engine_unittest.cc, 
&gt; chrome/services/speech/soda_speech_recognizer_impl_unittest.cc, 
&gt; chrome/services/speech/speech_recognition_recognizer_impl_unittest.cc, and 
&gt; services/on_device_model/on_device_model_service_unittest.cc).
&gt;
&gt; Flag name on about://flags
&gt;
&gt; enable-experimental-web-platform-features
&gt;
&gt; Finch feature name
&gt;
&gt; WebSpeechTimestamps
&gt;
&gt; Rollout plan
&gt;
&gt; Will ship enabled for all users
&gt;
&gt; Requires code in //chrome?
&gt;
&gt; True
&gt;
&gt; While the WebIDL surface and result plumbing live in //third_party/blink 
&gt; and //content/browser/speech, the on-device speech recognition backends and 
&gt; model management that supply segment timestamps (SODA in 
&gt; //chrome/services/speech and Optimization Guide / on-device model 
&gt; integration in //chrome/browser/speech) currently live in //chrome.
&gt;
&gt; Tracking bug
&gt;
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://crbug.com/528037568"&gt;https://crbug.com/528037568&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; Estimated milestones
&gt;
&gt; Shipping on desktop
&gt;
&gt; 159
&gt;
&gt; DevTrial on desktop
&gt;
&gt; 153
&gt;
&gt; Anticipated spec changes
&gt;
&gt; Open questions about a feature may be a source of future web compat or 
&gt; interop issues. Please list open issues (e.g. links to known github issues 
&gt; in the project for the feature specification) whose resolution may 
&gt; introduce web compat/interop risk (e.g., changing to naming or structure of 
&gt; the API in a non-backward-compatible way).
&gt;
&gt; None. Following W3C TAG (
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1267"&gt;https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1267&lt;/a&gt; ) and Audio WG/CG 
&gt; review on PR #192 (&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WebAudio/web-speech-api/pull/192"&gt;https://github.com/WebAudio/web-speech-api/pull/192&lt;/a&gt; ), 
&gt; the attribute names (speechStartTime and speechEndTime), type and units, 
&gt; and SpeechRecognitionEvent.timeStamp behavior have already been updated to 
&gt; match reviewer consensus. No further backward-incompatible spec changes are 
&gt; anticipated.
&gt;
&gt; Link to entry on the Chrome Platform Status
&gt;
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5811907077472256?gate=4580112537354240"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/feature/5811907077472256?gate=4580112537354240&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; Links to previous Intent discussions
&gt;
&gt; Intent to Prototype: 
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/r78IyGSnclg"&gt;https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/r78IyGSnclg&lt;/a&gt;
