&lt;div class="msgHead"&gt; &lt;h1&gt; &lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Intent+to+Experiment%5C%3A+Opening+links+in+a+split+tab%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;[blink-dev] Intent to Experiment: Opening links in a split tab&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/h1&gt; &lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt; &lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Mason+Freed%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Mason Freed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20261109" rel="nofollow"&gt;Mon, 09 Nov 2026 14:47:22 -0800&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;*Contact emails* &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="91fcf0e2bfbfbfd1f2f9e3fefcf8e4fcbffee3f6"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
*Explainer* &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/mfreed7/split-tabs"&gt;https://github.com/mfreed7/split-tabs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;
*Specification* *No information provided*
*Summary* Split screen scenarios are increasingly common. In addition to dual screen devices (i.e. physical split screen), many browsers have a split tab (i.e. virtual split screen) feature, where two tabs are tiled side-by-side within a single browser window. When using a split tab, there are multiple cases in which users want to open a link and view it side-by-side with the source page. Today there is no way for a web author to request that a navigation open into a split tab. The existing navigation targets (_blank, _self, _parent, _top) cannot express this, and windowFeatures only offers popup, which opens a separate, detached browser window. Without popup, window.open() opens the content as a new full-size tab in the current window, which is the only other option available. This feature provides methods (imperative and declarative) for web authors to request that a link open in a split tab, alongside the current page.
*Blink component* Blink&gt;DOM &lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3EDOM%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3EDOM%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
*Web Feature ID* Missing feature
*Search tags* window.open &lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/features#tags:window.open"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/features#tags:window.open&lt;/a&gt;&gt;, split tab &lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/features#tags:split%20tab"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/features#tags:split%20tab&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
*TAG review* &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1309"&gt;https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1309&lt;/a&gt;
*TAG review status* Pending
*Goals for experimentation* None
*Risks*
*Interoperability and Compatibility* There should be no compat risks, since these are new window feature values and a new attribute. (Extremely small, and acceptable, risk that existing content already uses the `windowFeatures` attribute.) The API also includes provisions for feature detection and easy progressive enhancement, such as the ability to explicitly fall back to popup behavior.
*Gecko*: No signal ( &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/1481"&gt;https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/1481&lt;/a&gt;)
*WebKit*: No signal ( &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/741"&gt;https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/741&lt;/a&gt;)
*Web developers*: Positive Private feedback is quite positive.
*Other signals*:
*WebView application risks*
Does this intent deprecate or change behavior of existing APIs, such that it has potentially high risk for Android WebView-based applications? *No information provided*
*Ongoing technical constraints* *No information provided*
*Debuggability* *No information provided*
*Will this feature be supported on all six Blink platforms (Windows, Mac, Linux, ChromeOS, Android, and Android WebView)?* No
*Is this feature fully tested by web-platform-tests &lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md"&gt;https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md&lt;/a&gt;&gt;?* No
*Flag name on about://flags* *No information provided*
*Finch feature name* WindowOpenSplitTab
*Requires code in //chrome?* False
*Tracking bug* &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://crbug.com/570412924"&gt;https://crbug.com/570412924&lt;/a&gt;
*Estimated milestones* DevTrial on desktop 158 DevTrial on Android 158
*Link to entry on the Chrome Platform Status* &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5136319775899648?gate=6263386169016320"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/feature/5136319775899648?gate=6263386169016320&lt;/a&gt;
*Links to previous Intent discussions* Intent to Prototype: &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msgid/blink-dev/CAM%3DNeDiY8jf6ETLNuj%2BXk%3DGJ89_NhUebFBBdNV9qMknZtiQhbQ%40mail.gmail.com"&gt;https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msgid/blink-dev/CAM%3DNeDiY8jf6ETLNuj%2BXk%3DGJ89_NhUebFBBdNV9qMknZtiQhbQ%40mail.gmail.com&lt;/a&gt;
This intent message was generated by Chrome Platform Status &lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/&lt;/a&gt;&gt;.
