&lt;pre&gt;Ugh, sorry. The chromestatus tool reminded me to fill in many blanks, but
not the basic ones like the version numbers and platform support. I've
updated the chromestatus page
&lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5136319775899648"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/feature/5136319775899648&lt;/a&gt;&gt; with more info now, but
see below for the specific answers.&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

On Mon, Nov 9, 2026 at 2:56 PM Yoav Weiss (@Shopify) &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="7c05131d0a0b195252523c1f140e131115091152130e1b"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
wrote:

&gt; On Mon, Nov 9, 2026 at 11:55 PM Yoav Weiss (@Shopify) &lt;
&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="621b0d031415074c4c4c22010a100d0f0b170f4c0d1005"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;
&gt;&gt; What milestones are you planning to run the experiment in?
&gt;&gt;
&gt;
Starting in M160 and going for 10 milestones. Sound ok?


&gt; *Will this feature be supported on all six Blink platforms (Windows, Mac,
&gt;&gt;&gt; Linux, ChromeOS, Android, and Android WebView)?*
&gt;&gt;&gt; No
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt; Can you elaborate on that?
&gt;

The elaboration is that I forgot to fill out that section. I've checked
that box, and added a bit more text about it. There's an important
distinction here - the APIs will be supported across all platforms. But not
all platforms (e.g. Android mobile) have a way to show split screens. On
those OS's, the fallback path will be taken, to a new tab.

Thanks,
Mason



