&lt;pre&gt;Contact emails &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="1378717271713d3d3d537e7a70617c607c75673d707c7e"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#ed868f8c8f8fc3c3c3ad80848e9f829e828b99c38e8280"&gt;mailto:&lt;span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="a0cbc2c1c2c28e8e8ee0cdc9c3d2cfd3cfc6d48ec3cfcd"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&gt;, &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="94fefbfcfafef5fabababad4f9fdf7e6fbe7fbf2e0baf7fbf9"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#1b71747375717a753535355b767278697468747d6f35787476"&gt;mailto:&lt;span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="355f5a5d5b5f545b1b1b1b75585c56475a465a53411b565a58"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;
Explainer &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/MicrosoftEdge/MSEdgeExplainers/blob/main/highlight-v2/explainer.md"&gt;https://github.com/MicrosoftEdge/MSEdgeExplainers/blob/main/highlight-v2/explainer.md&lt;/a&gt;
Specification No information provided
Summary Adds support for animations, transitions, and opacity to all CSS highlight pseudos including custom highlights. Adds support for minor per-range variances to custom highlights. Taken together, these additions enable developers to create staggered text entry effects without needing to subdivide text into spans.
Blink component Blink&gt;CSS&lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ECSS%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ECSS%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
Web Feature ID Missing feature
Motivation Many Web experiences apply visual effects to text. Streaming text experiences such as AI chat interfaces and online presentation tools have made text entry and exit effects especially prominent, while read-along experiences and editing tools use changing highlights to convey playback or analysis state. Existing Web primitives can be inefficient for text-level animation effects because they require backing elements. For a per-word animation with a moderate amount of text, hundreds of extra DOM elements would need to be created for no other reason than to support such an effect. This has negative implications on CPU and memory, and authors must do extra work for accessibility. The Custom Highlight API already lets authors identify and style arbitrary text ranges without changing the document structure. However, highlight styling has limitations that make it an incomplete replacement for element-level effects. This feature closes the gaps for text entry effects by adding opacity, animations and transitions, and support for minor per-range style variations to highlights.
Initial public proposal &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14613"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14613&lt;/a&gt;
Goals for experimentation None
Tracking bug &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues/579833788"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues/579833788&lt;/a&gt;
Estimated milestones No milestones specified
