&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Rick+Byers%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Rick Byers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20261007" rel="nofollow"&gt;Wed, 07 Oct 2026 08:28:45 -0700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;It looks like this was removed from the spec here
&lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WICG/local-network-access/commit/314cb7ad46d6c10a9498551a445a7cd7f3cfbc0c"&gt;https://github.com/WICG/local-network-access/commit/314cb7ad46d6c10a9498551a445a7cd7f3cfbc0c&lt;/a&gt;&gt;,
so I've added that as the spec link.&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

Please request the additional reviews required for deprecation and removal
(we upgraded the chromestatus entry from just 'plan' to a full removal
since it appears that's what you're asking for).

I assume this will have a killswitch, just in case some enterprise was
somehow relying on it or something, right?

LGTM2 conditional on the above.

Rick

