&lt;div class="msgHead"&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;
&lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22Re%5C%3A+%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Re%5C%3A+Intent+to+Deprecate+and+Remove%5C%3A+RemoveTreatAsPublicAddress%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Re: [blink-dev] Re: Intent to Deprecate and Remove: RemoveTreatAsPublicAddress&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Hubert+Chao%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Hubert Chao&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20261007" rel="nofollow"&gt;Wed, 07 Oct 2026 09:03:13 -0700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;Set the stage; requested all of the prepare to ship approvals. I'll post
here when I have all of the approvals.&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

Forgot this was added to the LNA spec, I will note that it was in the LNA
spec for less than 3 weeks (added Jun 15, 2026 here
&lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WICG/local-network-access/commit/345eafde94fe9a3f81d29f6bed6d055643cd4717"&gt;https://github.com/WICG/local-network-access/commit/345eafde94fe9a3f81d29f6bed6d055643cd4717&lt;/a&gt;&gt;,
then removed Jul 6, 2026 here
&lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WICG/local-network-access/commit/92657b3869920d973aea00c93e861c4b8751bda9"&gt;https://github.com/WICG/local-network-access/commit/92657b3869920d973aea00c93e861c4b8751bda9&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
).

It was in the PNA spec (here
&lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wicg.github.io/private-network-access/#csp"&gt;https://wicg.github.io/private-network-access/#csp&lt;/a&gt;&gt;); the LNA spec copied
the PNA text for the three-week period when we thought we would keep it,
before deciding to remove it entirely.

/hubert


On Wed, Oct 7, 2026 at 11:32 AM Rick Byers &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="84f6e6fdaaaaaac4e7ecf6ebe9edf1e9aaebf6e3"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:

&gt; Actually sorry, it looks like we aren't able to correct the stage for you
&gt; in the tool. Please set the stage to &quot;prepare to ship&quot;, the tool will
&gt; require you to get (for example) Enterprise approval for shipping a
&gt; breaking change.
&gt;
&gt; Rick
&gt;
&gt; On Wed, Oct 7, 2026 at 5:27 PM Rick Byers &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="7200100b5c5c5c32111a001d1f1b071f5c1d0015"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;
&gt;&gt; It looks like this was removed from the spec here
&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WICG/local-network-access/commit/314cb7ad46d6c10a9498551a445a7cd7f3cfbc0c"&gt;https://github.com/WICG/local-network-access/commit/314cb7ad46d6c10a9498551a445a7cd7f3cfbc0c&lt;/a&gt;&gt;,
&gt;&gt; so I've added that as the spec link.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Please request the additional reviews required for deprecation and
&gt;&gt; removal (we upgraded the chromestatus entry from just 'plan' to a full
&gt;&gt; removal since it appears that's what you're asking for).
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; I assume this will have a killswitch, just in case some enterprise was
&gt;&gt; somehow relying on it or something, right?
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; LGTM2 conditional on the above.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Rick
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; On Wed, Oct 7, 2026 at 5:20 PM Chris Harrelson &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="95f6fde7fce6bbbbbbd5f6fde7faf8fce0f8bbfae7f2"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; LGTM1
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; On Wed, Sep 30, 2026 at 12:25 PM Hubert Chao &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="6a02094444442a0902180507031f074405180d"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; One thing that may not be clear: the plan here is to remove the header
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; directly without a deprecation trial.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; On Wednesday, September 30, 2026 at 3:22:59 PM UTC-4 Chromestatus wrote:
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Contact emails*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="28404b060606684b405a4745415d4506475a4f"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Explainer*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Specification*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Summary*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; The Content Security Policy header treat-as-public-address was added
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; as part of Private Network Access to allow non-documents to declare
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; themselves as being in the public address space (
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wicg.github.io/private-network-access/#csp"&gt;https://wicg.github.io/private-network-access/#csp&lt;/a&gt;). It is primarily
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; useful for testing.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WICG/private-network-access/issues/88"&gt;https://github.com/WICG/private-network-access/issues/88&lt;/a&gt; highlights
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; some issues with this header, and the decision was made to remove this
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; header instead of moving it somewhere else. For testing use cases, the
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; --ip-address-space-overrides command line flag can be used. This header 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; was
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; only ever implemented in Chromium; Firefox has never implemented this
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; header and has no plans to. Safari has not implemented Private Network
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Access or Local Network Access and so does not have the header either.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Blink component*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Blink &gt; SecurityFeature &gt; LocalNetworkAccess
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%20%3E%20SecurityFeature%20%3E%20LocalNetworkAccess%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%20%3E%20SecurityFeature%20%3E%20LocalNetworkAccess%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Web Feature ID*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; local-network-access
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://webstatus.dev/features/local-network-access"&gt;https://webstatus.dev/features/local-network-access&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Motivation*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Header does not fit well into Content Security Policy, and it was
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; deemed unnecessary given the alternative of using
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; `--ip-address-space-overrides` Metrics show this is barely used:
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/metrics/feature/timeline/popularity/5983"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/metrics/feature/timeline/popularity/5983&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Initial public proposal*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Goals for experimentation*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; None
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Debuggability*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Requires code in //chrome?*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; False
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Tracking bug*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues/527730705"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues/527730705&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Estimated milestones*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; No milestones specified
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Link to entry on the Chrome Platform Status*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5187021965492224?gate=5964820426915840"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/feature/5187021965492224?gate=5964820426915840&lt;/a&gt;
