&lt;div class="msgHead"&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;
&lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22Re%5C%3A+%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Re%5C%3A+Intent+to+Ship%5C%3A+WebGPU%5C%3A+Texture+Compression+Unaligned%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Re: [blink-dev] Re: Intent to Ship: WebGPU: Texture Compression Unaligned&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Alex+Russell%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Alex Russell&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20260923" rel="nofollow"&gt;Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:12:00 -0700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;Thanks for clarifying, Corentin. LGTM3.

On Wednesday, September 23, 2026 at 8:06:03 AM UTC-7 Vladimir Levin wrote:&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

&gt; LGTM2. I think you already filled out the Adoption gate, but can you also 
&gt; request review (or NA) for it as well
&gt;
&gt; On Wednesday, September 23, 2026 at 10:59:26 AM UTC-4 Rick Byers wrote:
&gt;
&gt;&gt; Seems like a minor (low-risk) but valuable change to me. LGTM1
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; On Mon, Sep 21, 2026 at 1:21 PM 'Corentin Wallez' via blink-dev &lt;
&gt;&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="a9cbc5c0c7c284cdccdfe9cac1dbc6c4c0dcc487c6dbce"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Hey Alex,
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Correct! It would improve the compression fidelity of these formats (so 
&gt;&gt;&gt; only the loss from the format is there, not the loss from resizing), which 
&gt;&gt;&gt; will allow uses in more places, resulting in GPU memory gains. (most 
&gt;&gt;&gt; commonly 4x, up to 16x).
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Cheers,
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Corentin
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; On Mon, Sep 21, 2026 at 8:48 PM Alex Russell &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="780b14111f100c1401565656381b100a1715110d1556170a1f"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Hey Corentin,
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; For those of us who are not in the WebGPU head-space all day, is it 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; fair to summarize this feature as improving memory use and compression 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; fidelity for certain GPU image formats?
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Best,
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Alex
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; On Friday, September 18, 2026 at 9:43:05 AM UTC-7 Chromestatus wrote:
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Contact emails*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="15766274793b3b3b55727a7a7279703b767a78"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Explainer*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://gpuweb.github.io/gpuweb/#dom-gpufeaturename-texture-compression-unaligned"&gt;https://gpuweb.github.io/gpuweb/#dom-gpufeaturename-texture-compression-unaligned&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Specification*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://gpuweb.github.io/gpuweb/#dom-gpufeaturename-texture-compression-unaligned"&gt;https://gpuweb.github.io/gpuweb/#dom-gpufeaturename-texture-compression-unaligned&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;  
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Summary*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Compressed texture (using the BC, ETC or ASTC formats) in unextended 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; WebGPU must have a size that's a multiple of the block size (4x4 or up to 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; 12x12). This is very constraining when compressing arbitrary images as a 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; resizing step must happen which looses high-frequency information. Most 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; hardware supports compressed textures with partial blocks at the border 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; such that the textures can have any size, removing this issue. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Blink component*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Blink&gt;WebGPU 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3EWebGPU%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3EWebGPU%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Web Feature ID*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; webgpu &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://webstatus.dev/features/webgpu"&gt;https://webstatus.dev/features/webgpu&lt;/a&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Motivation*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Compressed texture (using the BC, ETC or ASTC formats) in unextended 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; WebGPU must have a size that's a multiple of the block size (4x4 or up to 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; 12x12). This is very constraining when compressing arbitrary images as a 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; resizing step must happen which looses high-frequency information. Most 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; hardware supports compressed textures with partial blocks at the border 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; such that the textures can have any size, removing this issue. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Initial public proposal*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/issues/2006"&gt;https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/issues/2006&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *TAG review*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided* 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *TAG review status*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Not applicable
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Goals for experimentation*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; None 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Risks*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Interoperability and Compatibility*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; This feature has been approved in W3C GPU for the Web WG meetings 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; including participants from Safari and Firefox. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Gecko*: No signal (&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/pull/6312"&gt;https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/pull/6312&lt;/a&gt;) 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Implementation 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; is ongoing &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/gfx-rs/wgpu/pull/10247"&gt;https://github.com/gfx-rs/wgpu/pull/10247&lt;/a&gt; Feedback 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; indicated via WebGPU standardization process.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *WebKit*: Positive (&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/pull/6312"&gt;https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/pull/6312&lt;/a&gt;) 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Specification 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; approval constitutes a positive signal, per 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/294#issuecomment-1877411933"&gt;https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/294#issuecomment-1877411933&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Web developers*: Positive (
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/issues/2006#issuecomment-2910632703"&gt;https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/issues/2006#issuecomment-2910632703&lt;/a&gt;) 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Bevy, 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Unity, Spark.js positive about this feature.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Other signals*:
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *WebView application risks*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Does this intent deprecate or change behavior of existing APIs, such 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; that it has potentially high risk for Android WebView-based applications? 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided* 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Debuggability*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided* 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Will this feature be supported on all six Blink platforms (Windows, 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Mac, Linux, ChromeOS, Android, and Android WebView)?*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Yes 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; All platforms have support, where hardware support is available. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Is this feature fully tested by web-platform-tests 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md"&gt;https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md&lt;/a&gt;&gt;?*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Yes 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; WebGPU/WGSL have a conformance test suite (
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/gpuweb/cts"&gt;https://github.com/gpuweb/cts&lt;/a&gt;) that is regularly pulled into Chromium 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; and part of the testing of Dawn/Tint in Chromium. While the CTS can be 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; embedded in WPT, the WebGPU team opted to keep it separate in Chromium 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; testing to use a customized harness for robustness and performance.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Flag name on about://flags*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided* 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Finch feature name*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; WebGPUEnabledEnabledToggles 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Rollout plan*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Will ship enabled for all users
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Requires code in //chrome?*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; False
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Tracking bug*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://crbug.com/528245806"&gt;https://crbug.com/528245806&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Estimated milestones*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; No milestones specified
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Anticipated spec changes*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Open questions about a feature may be a source of future web compat or 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; interop issues. Please list open issues (e.g. links to known github 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; issues 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; in the project for the feature specification) whose resolution may 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; introduce web compat/interop risk (e.g., changing to naming or structure 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; of 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; the API in a non-backward-compatible way). 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Link to entry on the Chrome Platform Status*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5080544005193728?gate=6068538249969664"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/feature/5080544005193728?gate=6068538249969664&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; This intent message was generated by Chrome Platform Status 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com"&gt;https://chromestatus.com&lt;/a&gt;&gt;. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; -- 
&gt;&gt;&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Groups &quot;blink-dev&quot; group.
&gt;&gt;&gt; To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send 
&gt;&gt;&gt; an email to &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="7e1c12171015531a1b08550b100d0b1c0d1d0c5050503e1d160c1113170b1350110c19"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;.
&gt;&gt;&gt; To view this discussion visit 
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msgid/blink-dev/CAGdfWNNnCVe5QWrHFrsjbUjcyYFiR5ZbhqB38bj27RCm4k_wZA%40mail.gmail.com"&gt;https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msgid/blink-dev/CAGdfWNNnCVe5QWrHFrsjbUjcyYFiR5ZbhqB38bj27RCm4k_wZA%40mail.gmail.com&lt;/a&gt;
