&lt;div class="msgHead"&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;
&lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Re%5C%3A+Intent+to+Ship%5C%3A+SVG+textPath+side+attribute%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;[blink-dev] Re: Intent to Ship: SVG textPath side attribute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Hyowon+Kim%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Hyowon Kim&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20260922" rel="nofollow"&gt;Tue, 22 Sep 2026 09:02:50 -0700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;Thanks Alex and Jeffrey.

I've filed an FYI with the TAG:
&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1279"&gt;https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1279&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

Apologies for the late notification.
I'll make sure to notify the TAG well before I2S in future.

Best,
Hyowon

On 2026-09-22 03:43, Jeffrey Yasskin wrote:
&gt; On Mon, Sep 21, 2026 at 11:42 AM Alex Russell
&gt; &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="03706f6a646b776f7a2d2d2d43606b716c6e6a766e2d6c7164"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt; 
&gt;&gt; LGTM1 with a nit that this is a case where we probably don't
&gt;&gt; anticipate the TAG providing substantive feedback, but which we want
&gt;&gt; to make them aware of. In such cases, we should send an FYI.
&gt;&gt; Regardless, we should send a note to the TAG well before I2S. Adding
&gt;&gt; Jeffery who can advise in case that's the wrong thing to do here.
&gt; 
&gt; That sounds right to me. 
&gt; 
&gt;&gt; Best,
&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt; Alex
&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt; On Wednesday, September 16, 2026 at 6:44:56 PM UTC-7 Chromestatus
&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Contact &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="ee8b838f87829d869781c0c0c0ae87898f82878fc08d8183"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Specification
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://w3c.github.io/svgwg/svg2-draft/text.html#TextPathElementSideAttribute"&gt;https://w3c.github.io/svgwg/svg2-draft/text.html#TextPathElementSideAttribute&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Summary The side attribute on the SVG &lt;textPath&gt; element places
&gt;&gt;&gt; text on the opposite side of the path, equivalent to reversing the
&gt;&gt;&gt; path direction. This lets authors label a shape's interior or
&gt;&gt;&gt; exterior (e.g. text inside vs. outside a circular path) without
&gt;&gt;&gt; duplicating or manually reversing path data. 
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Blink component Blink&gt;SVG [1]
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Web Feature ID svg-textPath-side [2] 
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Motivation Authors placing text along a path have no way to flip
&gt;&gt;&gt; which side of the path the text appears on. The side attribute
&gt;&gt;&gt; lets authors write side=&quot;right&quot; to place text on the opposite side
&gt;&gt;&gt; of the path, without duplicating or reversing the path data. This
&gt;&gt;&gt; helps label both the inside and outside of a shape, such as a
&gt;&gt;&gt; circular path, with different text on each side. 
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Initial public proposal _No information provided_
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; TAG review Not yet requested. This implements an existing SVG2
&gt;&gt;&gt; attribute with a WG resolution and shipping Firefox precedent; TAG
&gt;&gt;&gt; review will be evaluated during Intent to Ship. 
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; TAG review status Not applicable
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Goals for experimentation None 
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Risks 
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Interoperability and Compatibility Firefox already shipped this
&gt;&gt;&gt; (Firefox 152):
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2034371"&gt;https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2034371&lt;/a&gt; WebKit has it
&gt;&gt;&gt; in progress (not merged yet):
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/66616"&gt;https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/66616&lt;/a&gt; The SVG Working Group
&gt;&gt;&gt; resolved to add IDL constants for side
&gt;&gt;&gt; (w3.org/2026/04/23-svg-minutes.html#2c4e [3]) 
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; _Gecko_: Shipped/Shipping
&gt;&gt;&gt; (&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2034371"&gt;https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2034371&lt;/a&gt;)
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; _WebKit_: In development
&gt;&gt;&gt; (&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/66616"&gt;https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/66616&lt;/a&gt;)
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; _Web developers_: No signals
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; _Other signals_:
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Security No new security concerns. The attribute only changes
&gt;&gt;&gt; where already-visible text is rendered along a path.
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; WebView application risks 
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Does this intent deprecate or change behavior of existing APIs,
&gt;&gt;&gt; such that it has potentially high risk for Android WebView-based
&gt;&gt;&gt; applications? _No information provided_ 
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Debuggability No special DevTools support needed. The side
&gt;&gt;&gt; attribute is visible and editable like any other SVG attribute in
&gt;&gt;&gt; the Elements panel. 
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Will this feature be supported on all six Blink platforms
&gt;&gt;&gt; (Windows, Mac, Linux, ChromeOS, Android, and Android WebView)?Yes
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Is this feature fully tested by web-platform-tests [4]? Yes 
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wpt.fyi/results/svg/types/scripted/SVGAnimatedEnumeration-SVGTextPathElement.html"&gt;https://wpt.fyi/results/svg/types/scripted/SVGAnimatedEnumeration-SVGTextPathElement.html&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wpt.fyi/results/svg/text/reftests/textpath-side-003.svg"&gt;https://wpt.fyi/results/svg/text/reftests/textpath-side-003.svg&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wpt.fyi/results/svg/text/reftests/textpath-side-005.svg"&gt;https://wpt.fyi/results/svg/text/reftests/textpath-side-005.svg&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Flag name on about://flags Experimental web platform features 
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Finch feature name SVGTextPathSideAttribute 
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Rollout plan Will ship enabled for all users
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Requires code in //chrome? False
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Tracking bug &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40362379"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40362379&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Estimated milestones
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Shipping on desktop
&gt;&gt;&gt; 156
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Shipping on Android
&gt;&gt;&gt; 156
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Shipping on WebView
&gt;&gt;&gt; 156
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Anticipated spec changes 
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Open questions about a feature may be a source of future web
&gt;&gt;&gt; compat or interop issues. Please list open issues (e.g. links to
&gt;&gt;&gt; known github issues in the project for the feature specification)
&gt;&gt;&gt; whose resolution may introduce web compat/interop risk (e.g.,
&gt;&gt;&gt; changing to naming or structure of the API in a
&gt;&gt;&gt; non-backward-compatible way). The SVG WG resolved to add IDL
&gt;&gt;&gt; constants for side, but this hasn't yet been reflected in the
&gt;&gt;&gt; published Editor's Draft text - an editorial gap, not an open
&gt;&gt;&gt; design question (&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/svgwg/issues/1086"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/svgwg/issues/1086&lt;/a&gt;).
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Link to entry on the Chrome Platform Status
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5422782593761280?gate=5533956580704256"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/feature/5422782593761280?gate=5533956580704256&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; Links to previous Intent discussionsIntent to Prototype:
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msgid/blink-dev/6a850bf7.a9d706b7.140c01.05e3.GAE%40google.com"&gt;https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msgid/blink-dev/6a850bf7.a9d706b7.140c01.05e3.GAE%40google.com&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; This intent message was generated by Chrome Platform Status [5].
&gt;  
&gt; 
&gt; Links:
&gt; ------
&gt; [1] &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ESVG%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ESVG%22&lt;/a&gt;
&gt; [2] &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://webstatus.dev/features/svg-textPath-side"&gt;https://webstatus.dev/features/svg-textPath-side&lt;/a&gt;
&gt; [3] &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://w3.org/2026/04/23-svg-minutes.html#2c4e"&gt;https://w3.org/2026/04/23-svg-minutes.html#2c4e&lt;/a&gt;
&gt; [4] 
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md"&gt;https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md&lt;/a&gt;
&gt; [5] &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com"&gt;https://chromestatus.com&lt;/a&gt;

