&lt;div class="msgHead"&gt; &lt;h1&gt; &lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Intent+to+Ship%5C%3A+Use+scroll%5C-snap%5C-type%5C%3A+pair+to+snap+to+a+single+element%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;[blink-dev] Intent to Ship: Use scroll-snap-type: pair to snap to a single element&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/h1&gt; &lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt; &lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Chromestatus%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Chromestatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20260922" rel="nofollow"&gt;Tue, 22 Sep 2026 09:13:43 -0700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Contact emails &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="8ee2edeaefa0a0a0cee9e1e1e9e2eba0ede1e3"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt; &lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;
Explainer &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/explainers-by-googlers/scroll-snap-type-pair"&gt;https://github.com/explainers-by-googlers/scroll-snap-type-pair&lt;/a&gt;
Specification &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-scroll-snap-1"&gt;https://drafts.csswg.org/css-scroll-snap-1&lt;/a&gt;
Summary &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/9519"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/9519&lt;/a&gt; Add a &quot;pair&quot; keyword to scroll-snap-type. If used, when the container scroll snaps to an element on one axis, it should snap to the same element on the other axis. In the existing spec, the &quot;both&quot; keyword allows the scroll container to select snap targets in X and Y axes independently and snap to different targets.
Blink component Blink&gt;Scroll
