&lt;div class="msgHead"&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;
&lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Re%5C%3A+Intent+to+Ship%5C%3A+JPEG+XL+decoding+support+%5C%28image%5C%2Fjxl%5C%29+in+blink%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;[blink-dev] Re: Intent to Ship: JPEG XL decoding support (image/jxl) in blink&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Sergey+Davidoff%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Sergey Davidoff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20260901" rel="nofollow"&gt;Tue, 01 Sep 2026 07:48:45 -0700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;A single large image is the best-case scenario for jxl-rs decoder, and is
easy to measure. According to Mozilla's intent to ship announcement, jxl-rs
performs even worse when decoding many small images, so this benchmark is
the best-case scenario for decoding performance.&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

вт, 1 сент. 2026 г. в 10:12, Aleksandr Ivanov &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="8beaa5a5a5cbe3eef3e6e4efeea5e4f9ec"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;:

&gt; Again, that's not a real scenario. No one in their sane mind would view
&gt; 100mpx lossless file for fun in the first place.
&gt;

-- 
