&lt;div class="msgHead"&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;
&lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22Re%5C%3A+%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Intent+to+Experiment%5C%3A+Opening+links+in+a+split+tab%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Experiment: Opening links in a split tab&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Yoav+Weiss+%5C%28%40Shopify%5C%29%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Yoav Weiss (@Shopify)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20261110" rel="nofollow"&gt;Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:23:54 -0800&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;On Tue, Nov 10, 2026 at 6:50 PM Mason Freed &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="8ce1edffa2a2a2ccefe4fee3e1e5f9e1a2e3feeb"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

&gt;
&gt; On Tue, Nov 10, 2026 at 8:27 AM Yoav Weiss (@Shopify) &lt;
&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="8ff6e0eef9f8eaa1a1a1cfece7fde0e2e6fae2a1e0fde8"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;
&gt;&gt; LGTM to experiment M160-M169
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; This is a super exciting feature, thanks for working on this!!
&gt;&gt;
&gt;
&gt; Thanks! Glad you like it.
&gt;
&gt;
&gt;&gt; On Tue, Nov 10, 2026 at 12:21 AM Mason Freed &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="96fbf7e5b8b8b8d6f5fee4f9fbffe3fbb8f9e4f1"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; The elaboration is that I forgot to fill out that section. I've checked
&gt;&gt;&gt; that box, and added a bit more text about it. There's an important
&gt;&gt;&gt; distinction here - the APIs will be supported across all platforms. But not
&gt;&gt;&gt; all platforms (e.g. Android mobile) have a way to show split screens. On
&gt;&gt;&gt; those OS's, the fallback path will be taken, to a new tab.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Is this a temporary gap or is it the planned end state?
&gt;&gt;
&gt;
&gt; I suppose it's temporary, but might be longer-term temporary. I don't have
&gt; immediate plans to expand the base browser split tabs feature, but if/when
&gt; that happens, this feature would immediately support them.
&gt;
&gt;
&gt;&gt; Would developers have a way to detect support (and fall back to other
&gt;&gt; primitives/experiences when the split tab experience is not supported)?
&gt;&gt;
&gt;
&gt; I talk a bit about feature detection in this section of the explainer
&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/mfreed7/split-tabs#feature-detection-navigatorsplittabsupported"&gt;https://github.com/mfreed7/split-tabs#feature-detection-navigatorsplittabsupported&lt;/a&gt;&gt;.
&gt; The short answer is that you can detect support for the API itself via
&gt; `&quot;windowFeatures&quot; in HTMLAnchorelement` or similar, but you can't (for
&gt; privacy reasons) detect a-priori whether you'll actually *get* a split tab.
&gt;

Interesting! What are the privacy reasons? The &quot;If the window is already
split&quot; case? Something else?


&gt; Thanks,
&gt; Mason
&gt;
&gt;
&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Thanks,
&gt;&gt;&gt; Mason
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Is this feature fully tested by web-platform-tests
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md"&gt;https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md&lt;/a&gt;&gt;?*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; No
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Flag name on about://flags*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Finch feature name*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; WindowOpenSplitTab
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Requires code in //chrome?*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; False
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Tracking bug*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://crbug.com/570412924"&gt;https://crbug.com/570412924&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Estimated milestones*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; DevTrial on desktop 158
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; DevTrial on Android 158
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Link to entry on the Chrome Platform Status*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5136319775899648?gate=6263386169016320"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/feature/5136319775899648?gate=6263386169016320&lt;/a&gt;
